{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779385848,"nonce":"Dsl0NafvCvPL/t12OGgVUaotRwM=","message":"## Child split: Workspace representation and runtime playback\n\nCreated two concrete child issues from the Workspace part of this umbrella:\n\n- `946c859` — Studio Workspace spatial representation and objective authoring contract.\n- `6a094c9` — Studio Workspace runtime playback and validation overlays.\n\nWhy split them:\n\n- `946c859` is the authoring contract. It documents that the current Workspace projection is still mostly schematic/mockup scaffolding, not a finished UX. It specifies provider/schema-backed spatial representations for tasks, mechanics, components, effectors, joints, links, task goals/distributions, and canonical interaction targets for objective creation.\n- `6a094c9` is the runtime/inspection contract. It covers validation/eval trajectory playback, sampled previews, live/progress overlays, checkpoint/rollout artifacts, and manifest-backed coordinate/task/mechanics metadata.\n\nImportant design point from `946c859`: schematic task objects can be visible without all being canonical objective targets. For example, a center-out task may show several target directions, but objective creation should canonicalize to the task's goal entity. Random rectangular reaches may be represented by schematic initial/target points or a distribution glyph. Point-mass mechanics, two-link arms, effectors, fixed/mobile joints, and future mechanics objects need consistent representation metadata rather than bespoke drawings.\n\nProvider implication: new tasks/mechanics/components should eventually declare or derive Workspace representation metadata through the Feedbax provider/schema contract. Mandible should not hardcode these renderings; it should consume provider capabilities or open the object in Feedbax Studio.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}